<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gold Fields Coal Q2 net profit 27.04m rand.</title>
<headline>Gold Fields Coal Q2 net profit 27.04m rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending  27.04 vs 18.39</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  31.75 vs 5.08</p>
<p>    Coal output (tonnes)		2,518,000 vs 2,271,000</p>
<p>    Coal sold (tonnes)		  2,417,000 vs 2,212,000</p>
<p>    Sales					 70.87 vs 77.69</p>
<p>    Cost of sales			     52.90 vs 65.34</p>
<p>Full name: Gold Fields Coal Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company awarded an interim dividend of 60 cents per share on June 10.</p>
<p>- Directors said shareholders registered on June 27</p>
<p>could elect to take capitalisation shares at a ratio of 64 cents to the average closing price for Gold Fields Coal shares for the three days ending July 24.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
